Disable rwsem optimistic owner spinning with Harmony virtual clocks

Linux's reader-owner rwsem optimistic spin loop uses sched_clock() for its
timeout. Harmony virtual clocks stop advancing during exit-free spinning, so
the loop can fail to reach its timeout and stall the outer runtime. Keep
contended rwsems on Linux's existing blocking and wakeup path; disable only
this optional owner-spin optimization in either Harmony virtual-clock kernel.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository's kernel-patch
exception.

---
--- a/kernel/Kconfig.locks
+++ b/kernel/Kconfig.locks
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ config MUTEX_SPIN_ON_OWNER
 
 config RWSEM_SPIN_ON_OWNER
        def_bool y
-       depends on SMP && ARCH_SUPPORTS_ATOMIC_RMW
+       depends on SMP && ARCH_SUPPORTS_ATOMIC_RMW && !HARMONY_PVCLOCK && !HARMONY_ARM_PVCLOCK
 
 config LOCK_SPIN_ON_OWNER
        def_bool y
